{"content":[{"c":["MESHEZABEEL*, MESHEZABEL"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Ancestor of Meshullam who helped repair the Jerusalem wall (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.4","r":"Neh.3.4","rawR":"Neh.3.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.4","value":"Neh.3.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:4"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Political leader who signed Ezra’s covenant of faithfulness to God during the postexilic period (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.10.21","r":"Neh.10.21","rawR":"Neh.10.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.10.21","value":"Neh.10.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 10:21"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Father of Pethahiah, an adviser to King Artaxerxes regarding the people in Judah (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.24","r":"Neh.11.24","rawR":"Neh.11.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.24","value":"Neh.11.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:24"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"MeshezabeelMeshezabel","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Neh 3:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.3.4","rawQueryValue":"Neh.3.4","sourceRefExact":"Neh.3.4"},{"anchorText":"Neh 10:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.10.21","rawQueryValue":"Neh.10.21","sourceRefExact":"Neh.10.21"},{"anchorText":"Neh 11:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.11.24","rawQueryValue":"Neh.11.24","sourceRefExact":"Neh.11.24"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"98f2930ed8dffaba460b09eed9eaa667f81608c7ed3bfc12c5609a66c9f3fcc7","sourceItemName":"MeshezabeelMeshezabel","sourceItemOrder":275,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"MeshezabeelMeshezabel","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Meshezabeel*, Meshezabel","tit